  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $G$ be a group and let $k\\geqslant 2$. Let $H_1,\\ldots,H_k$ be subgroups of $G$, and $g_1,\\ldots,g_k$ elements of $G$ such that the cosets $g_1H_1,\\ldots,g_kH_k$ form a partition of $G$. Is it true that $|G:H_i|=|G:H_j|$ for some $i\\ne j$?",
